cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "MCP Conduct Register: a machine generated register of measured MCP server conduct"
message: "If you cite or quote this register, please cite it as below. The measurement records themselves are facts and are not claimed as property."
type: dataset
authors:
  - family-names: Oga
    given-names: Toshikatsu
    alias: ogasurfproject-jpg
    affiliation: "The HORIZONs Co., Ltd."
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0009-0000-9180-903X"
    country: JP
doi: "10.5281/zenodo.21970931"
repository-code: "https://github.com/ogasurfproject-jpg/mcp-conduct-register"
url: "https://shield.the-horizons-innovation.com/verify-directory/"
abstract: >-
  A register of Model Context Protocol (MCP) servers that records what was
  measured rather than what anyone recommends. Rows are generated daily from a
  public API by a script with no editorial input. Every verdict carries a
  SHA-256 that any third party can recompute from the published bytes, and the
  accumulated records are anchored to Bitcoin through OpenTimestamps. Records
  unflattering to the operator are retained, including failures of the
  operator's own servers, because the code contains no route for removing them.
keywords:
  - Model Context Protocol
  - MCP
  - AI agents
  - transparency log
  - verifiable records
  - OpenTimestamps
  - Bitcoin anchoring
  - vendor neutral registry
license: MIT
